  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2fce283e6d2030d42a8c34fc2e538818, type: 3}
  m_Name: Pop Culture 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: The film "The Sound of Music" was so popular in South Korea, one movie
    theater did what to take advantage of it's popularity?
  answers:
  - Paid to have the movie dubbed in Korean
  - Cut out all of the musical numbers
  - Hired a band to play along with the film
  - Showed the film 24 hours a day
  correctAnswerIndex: 1
  explanation: 'The theater owner decided to cut out all of the musical numbers in
    order to shorten the runtime of the film, allowing it to be show more times in
    a day. '
